# OmniVoice source and model-resource review

Reviewed: 2026-10-25. Source: [k2-fsa/OmniVoice](https://github.com/k2-fsa/OmniVoice), commit [08be0b4ccbac3e13e374e86fbfead4b4cac343e2](https://github.com/k2-fsa/OmniVoice/commit/08be0b4ccbac3e13e374e86fbfead4b4cac343e2), committed 2026-08-24. Model snapshot: [c5fdb5ccb189668d56333f77ba2629f4cd7535f4](https://huggingface.co/k2-fsa/OmniVoice/tree/c5fdb5ccb189668d56333f77ba2629f4cd7535f4). Related: [media processing](../media-processing.md), [generation](../generation.md), [models](../models.md).

Identity matters: GitHub identifies [echonerve/omnivoice](https://github.com/echonerve/omnivoice) as a distinct fork of the original repository, not its renamed canonical location. Preserve original IDs and source provenance. A similar name or a search result ranking is not rename evidence.

The actionable API is `OmniVoice.from_pretrained(local_directory, device_map=..., dtype=...)`, followed by `generate(text=..., ref_audio=..., ref_text=...)`. [Loading lines333–371](https://github.com/k2-fsa/OmniVoice/blob/08be0b4ccbac3e13e374e86fbfead4b4cac343e2/omnivoice/models/omnivoice.py#L333-L371) shows independently loaded text tokenizer, audio tokenizer and feature extractor. Missing `audio_tokenizer/` triggers a fallback to another remote repository. MPS places that codec on CPU. Passing a local main checkpoint alone therefore does not guarantee offline execution or single-device inference.

An offline adapter should require all model, tokenizer and codec assets before launch, pin the resource manifest, disable network access and fail on absent dependencies. Supply the reference transcript explicitly so optional ASR is unnecessary. Return the actual codec sampling rate and inspect generated samples before creating a PCM WAV. Run inference in an isolated worker with bounded input/output and scoped cancellation; model import may load trusted package code, so packageRoot is a trusted configuration boundary. Hardware selections remain explicit, and source support is not proof that a given machine can execute the model.

The [pinned model card](https://huggingface.co/k2-fsa/OmniVoice/blob/c5fdb5ccb189668d56333f77ba2629f4cd7535f4/README.md) distinguishes Apache 2.0 code from CC-BY-NC pretrained weights. The bundled [audio-tokenizer license](https://huggingface.co/k2-fsa/OmniVoice/blob/c5fdb5ccb189668d56333f77ba2629f4cd7535f4/audio_tokenizer/LICENSE) is the Boson Higgs Audio 2 Community License, incorporating additional terms. A single Apache label for the assembled inference bundle is wrong. Retain the exact model and codec license documents in a provisioning manifest and check the intended use before enabling that bundle.

Adoption: an optional preprovisioned local reference-conditioned backend, especially for evaluating language coverage absent from smaller fixed-voice engines. The model card's 646-language coverage is a vendor claim, not measured quality across 646 languages. Its file size is storage, not a RAM/VRAM requirement. No weights were downloaded, no local inference or accelerator compatibility was tested, and no evidence here makes it a generally licensed commercial replacement for hosted cloning.
